{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794600395,"nonce":"yYaQDpkcyqpKFQeXFFqJgGDP6lI=","title":"Check the occluded-window handling for a minimized window, another Space and screen capture on macOS","message":"f9170ae drops frames while winit reports Occluded(true). Verified only with a maximized second window over the first: no Frame events while covered, a redraw and normal frame costs after the uncover.\n\nNot checked, each of which winit reports as Occluded on macOS:\n- A minimized window, and the same window restored.\n- A window on another Space, and returning to it.\n- The app hidden with Cmd-H.\n- A window that opens already occluded: the first frame waits for Occluded(false).\n- Screen capture or a screenshot tool reading a covered window: it will not update while covered.\n- A modal window over its parent, and a second window of the same app covering the first.\nThese need a person at the machine to cover, minimize and switch, so they were not driven from here.","files":null}]}